</section>
<section id="Sx4.SSx4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Ablation on Embedding Gating</h3>

<div id="Sx4.SSx4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ablation study in Table <a href="#Sx4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Effectiveness of element-wise multiplication ‣ Ablation on Embedding Gating ‣ Performance Evaluation ‣ EG-MLA: Embedding-Gated Multi-head Latent Attention for Scalable and Efficient LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reveals two critical observations about the design of the embedding gating mechanism.</p>
</div>
<section id="Sx4.SSx4.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">The Critical Role of Layer Normalization</h4>

<div id="Sx4.SSx4.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx4.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, the presence of LayerNorm after the gating operation is essential. Its removal leads to a clear degradation in performance, suggesting that normalization is crucial for stabilizing the gated feature distribution and ensuring effective downstream attention computation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx4.SSx4.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Effectiveness of element-wise multiplication</h4>

<div id="Sx4.SSx4.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx4.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Second, replacing the element-wise multiplication with simple addition results in a noticeable loss increase, although not as severe as removing LayerNorm. This indicates that the element-wise multiplicative interaction plays a more effective role in modulating key-value representations, likely because it enables fine-grained, dimension-wise control over the information flow.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx4.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx4.SSSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Overall, these findings reinforce the importance of both architectural choices—the normalization step and multiplicative gating—in maximizing the benefits of the embedding-guided modulation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<div id="Sx4.T3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:505.9pt;height:116.3pt;vertical-align:-53.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(119.8pt,-27.5pt) scale(1.90027621460977,1.90027621460977) ;">
<table id="Sx4.T3.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
